    {
      "_id": "Z3zNks0hi5mHZM3v",
      "_key": "!actors.items!07d4vAfCzD7Kk3Hj.Z3zNks0hi5mHZM3v",
      "name": "Shattered Form",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>When the jinn is reduced to 0 Hit Points, or it takes 35+ Bludgeoning damage on a single turn, the vessels containing it shatter, leaving their shards to swirl in a cloud of dust. The jinn's current Hit Point total resets to 127 Hit Points, its creature type changes from Construct to Undead, its AC becomes 15, it gains Immunity to the Grappled and Restrained conditions, it loses its Resonant Vessels trait, it can't use its Blast Off Bonus Action, and it gains the Ceramic Whirlwind trait until the jinn finishes a Short or Long Rest. Award a party an additional 7,200 XP (14,400 XP total) for defeating the jinn after its Shattered Form activates.</p><p>Once the jinn's Shattered Form has activated, it can't do so again until the jinn finishes a Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Ceramic Whirlwind.</strong> The jinn can move through a space as narrow as 1 foot without expending extra movement to do so, and it can move through the spaces of other creatures. When it moves through the space of another creature for the first time on a turn, that creature is subjected to the following effect. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 15 Dexterity. <em>Failure:</em> 7 (2d6) Slashing damage and 13 (3d8) damage of the type associated with the jinn's body (see Elements of Divinity trait).</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "type": {
          "value": "monster",
          "subtype": ""
        },
